// Practice quiz: Lazy and eager loading
// Unreviewed first draft, 2026-11-04. Formative, low-stakes retention practice. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: spring-boot/relationships-and-transactions/lazy-and-eager-loading

::o1 defaults::What is the default fetch type of @ManyToOne? {
=EAGER#Correct. To-one associations default to EAGER.
~LAZY#Not quite. To-many associations default to LAZY.
~None; you must set it#Not quite. JPA defines a default.
~It depends on the database#Not quite. The specification defines it.
}

::o1 collection default::When is a default @OneToMany collection loaded? {
=When it is first read, inside an open persistence context#Correct. It defaults to LAZY.
~When the application starts#Not quite. Nothing loads rows at startup.
~Always with the owner#Not quite. That is EAGER.
~Only when written to#Not quite. Reading also triggers it.
}

::o2 exception cause::What causes LazyInitializationException? {
=Reading a lazy association after the session closed#Correct. There is no context left to run the query.
~A missing foreign key#Not quite. That is a different problem.
~Too many rows#Not quite. Row count does not cause it.
~A wrong column type#Not quite. That fails differently.
}

::o2 open in view::What does the Boot default for spring.jpa.open-in-view do to lazy reads in web requests? {
=It keeps the context open, hiding many lazy failures#Correct. SQL can then run during rendering.
~It disables all lazy loading#Not quite. Lazy loading still works.
~It makes every association EAGER#Not quite. It does not change fetch types.
~It closes the session earlier#Not quite. It does the opposite.
}

::o3 choosing a fix::One endpoint needs sessions, and most callers do not. What is the best approach? {
=Keep the mapping lazy and fetch explicitly for that endpoint#Correct. Only that use case pays for it.
~Make the association EAGER#Not quite. Every caller pays for it.
~Disable SQL logging#Not quite. That hides information.
~Remove the association#Not quite. The endpoint still needs the data.
}

